# Listener-id separation

The mapping table and `StatsListenerService` are read only inside
`packages/orm/src/services/stats/listenerIdentity/`. The listener entity
(`packages/orm/src/entities/stats/statsListener.ts`) and its registration in
`packages/orm/src/db/entities.ts` name the table for TypeORM. Zone services exported from
`@podverse/orm` take an `account_id` and never return a `listener_id`.

Workers, management API and web, popularity readers, the range-totals refresh, and recommendation
jobs work from `listener_id` values already stored in event and taste rows.

Flagged listeners (`stats_flagged_listener`) and their too-soon signal (`stats_flag_signal`) are
keyed by `listener_id`. Management lists and clears flags by row id and `listener_id` and never
looks up or shows an account for them.

The read-only database role cannot select the mapping. Zone code uses the read-write data source.

The management database browser never lists `stats_listener`. Which event, taste, daily, and range
tables it lists is set in `apps/management-api/src/lib/database/tablePolicy.ts`.

User-facing copy calls the id pseudonymous at most, never anonymous or anonymized.

Enforcement is the `no-restricted-imports` block in `eslint.config.mjs` and
`statsListenerSeparation.sourceGuard.test.ts`. Adding a reader outside the zone means changing
this rule first. The import block and the source-guard allowlist follow that change.

Data model and contracts: `docs/features/POPULARITY-AND-TASTE-PROFILE.md`.
